  "answer_markdown": "## TrailFold — weekly client update\n\n### 30-day performance snapshot\nThese are **30-day comparisons**, not a weekly trend or a controlled experiment.\n\n- Sessions increased from 20,000 to 25,000 (**+25%**), while orders fell from 600 to 500 (**−16.7%**).\n- Net product revenue fell from $54,000 to $45,000 (**−16.7%**). Average revenue per order remained approximately **$90**.\n- Session-based conversion fell from **3.0% to 2.0%** (**−33.3%**).\n- The largest visible weakness is mobile: mobile conversion fell from **2.67% to 1.50%**, while desktop remained **4.0%** in both periods.\n- Add-to-cart sessions were flat at 10% of sessions. Checkout starts fell from 60% to 50% of add-to-cart sessions; orders per checkout start remained 50%. These are session-based counts, so they identify where to investigate rather than proving a user-level cause.\n\n### What the Meta/Shopify discrepancy means\nMeta reported $70,400 of purchase value on $22,000 spend, or **3.2x reported ROAS**, versus $54,000 on $18,000 spend, or **3.0x** previously. However, Shopify records only $45,000 of current-period net product revenue. Meta therefore reports **$25,400 more purchase value than Shopify revenue** for the current 30 days. The prior periods happened to match at $54,000, but that does not validate the current attribution.\n\nThe systems use different attribution windows and definitions: Meta uses 7-day click/1-day view, Klaviyo uses 5-day click/5-day open, and Meta value has not been reconciled to Shopify orders. The gap can include attribution overlap, view-through credit, returning-customer orders, timing, or configuration differences. We should not scale spend based on Meta ROAS until it reconciles to Shopify/P&L data. No revenue uplift is being claimed.\n\n## Three priorities\n1. **Reconcile channel reporting to Shopify and contribution economics.** Build one current-period view using Shopify net revenue, ad spend, product/delivery costs, and new-versus-returning orders. Treat Meta and Klaviyo attributed revenue as directional until reconciled.\n2. **Investigate the mobile conversion and checkout drop.** Update the PDP’s opening message to “An 18L daypack for workdays and short trips,” move the 13-inch laptop-sleeve specification and 4–7 business-day delivery estimate above reviews, and state “water-resistant, not waterproof.” Do not claim 15-inch laptop compatibility until confirmed.\n3. **Protect Daypack availability while improving qualified demand.** At the current 8 units/day velocity, 210 units provide about 26 days of coverage; replenishment arrives in 35 days. Do not increase Daypack acquisition spend now. The go decision is: proceed only when the owner confirms a stock/fulfilment plan covering the estimated gap and measurement is reconciled; otherwise hold incremental spend and use existing inventory for controlled creative/PDP learning only.\n\n## Decisions needed from the owner\n- Approve the proposed PDP headline, specification placement, and plain-language water-resistance clarification; approve or provide verified 15-inch laptop dimensions.\n- Approve the inventory-aware no-scale rule for Daypack spend and confirm whether any units are reserved for wholesale, replacements, or other commitments.\n- Approve access to Shopify order exports and ad/email spend data for a reconciled contribution view. No discount is proposed.\n\n## Internal task board\n| Task | Owner | Dependency | Acceptance check | Hours |\n|---|---|---|---|---:|\n| Reconcile Shopify, Meta, and Klaviyo period totals; separate new/returning where available | Owner | Shopify export and spend definitions | One table showing net revenue, orders, spend, attributed revenue, and unexplained variance | 2 |\n| Calculate Daypack coverage and document spend go/no-go status | Owner | Confirmed inventory commitments and reservations | Coverage uses 8/day, 35-day arrival, and a clearly stated gap/risk; status is “hold incremental spend” unless approved plan exists | 1 |\n| Approve PDP changes and verify laptop-fit wording | Owner | Product specification confirmation | Written approval or corrections supplied to designer/developer | 1 |\n| Produce mobile-first PDP hero/specification layout | Designer | Owner-approved copy | Design contains approved headline, 18L, 13-inch sleeve, water-resistant—not waterproof, and delivery estimate above reviews | 4 |\n| Produce laptop-fit comparison creative without unsupported claims | Designer | Verified dimensions or explicit 13-inch-only wording | Two variants delivered with no 15-inch claim and clear product context | 2 |\n| Prepare controlled mobile PDP/checkout implementation | Developer | Approved design and copy | Changes staged, mobile QA completed, and no checkout or shipping-policy regression found | 3 |\n| Add measurement notes/events for PDP view, add-to-cart, and checkout-start review | Developer | Access to Shopify theme/analytics setup | Event definitions documented; no claim of incrementality | 1 |\n",
